{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdsXmNEY3YCB6V1aakbe9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LnZHjweXAFWmBrFW1WZtP9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/e6-t05/primary/exec-ws/ea-behavior-statement.md","content":"# E-A: Behavior statement — migrate.md vs transform.py over probes.json\n\nEvidence requirement E-A: a statement of every behavior on the probe set where\nmigrate.md either does not determine the output or determines it differently\nfrom transform.py, or an explicit argument that none exists.\n\nAnalysis performed in-session at node `observe-evidence` by reading\n`package/artifacts/migrate.md`, `package/artifacts/transform.py`, and\n`package/artifacts/probes.json`. No access restriction applies to this\nanalysis (per Q1 admissibility constraints).\n\n## Reference semantics of transform.py\n\n```python\ndef transform(s):\n    s = s.strip()\n    m, d, y = s.split(\"/\")\n    y = int(y)\n    if y < 100:\n        y = 2000 + y if y < 50 else 1900 + y\n    return f\"{y:04d}-{int(m):02d}-{int(d):02d}\"\n```\n\n- Strips surrounding whitespace from the whole input.\n- Splits on `/` into exactly three components.\n- Two-digit-year pivot: `y < 50` → `2000 + y`; `50 <= y < 100` → `1900 + y`.\n- Years `>= 100` used as-is; output `YYYY-MM-DD` with zero-padded month/day\n  and `%04d` year.\n\n## Reference semantics of migrate.md\n\n- Input form `M/D/YY` or `M/D/YYYY`, month/day one or two digits.\n- Month and day zero-padded to two digits in output.\n- Two-digit years: **70–99 → 19xx, 00–69 → 20xx**.\n- Four-digit years used as-is.\n- `transform(s)` returns the ISO string. Nothing is said about whitespace,\n  malformed input, or any other input outside the stated form.\n\n## Complete enumeration of behaviors exercised by the probe set\n\nEach of the 12 probes exercises only behaviors in the following six classes.\nProbe indices are 0-based, in file order of probes.json.\n\n| # | Behavior | Probes exercising it | Classification |\n|---|----------|----------------------|----------------|\n| B1 | Parse `M/D/YY` / `M/D/YYYY` with 1–2 digit month/day, `/` separator | all (0–11) | Determined identically: migrate.md fixes the form; transform.py splits on `/` and integer-parses each component. |\n| B2 | Zero-pad month and day to two digits in output | 0,2,5,6,7,8 (1-digit components); 1,3,4,9,10,11 (already 2-digit) | Determined identically: migrate.md mandates padding; transform.py uses `:02d`. |\n| B3 | Four-digit year passed through unchanged | 1 (`1984`), 6 (`2024`), 11 (`1969`) | Determined identically (\"used as-is\" vs `y >= 100` branch + `%04d`). |\n| B4a | Two-digit years 70–99 → 19xx | 0 (`99`), 3 (`76`), 9 (`70`) | Determined identically (70–99 → 19xx; transform.py: `y >= 50` → `1900+y`). |\n| B4b | Two-digit years 00–49 → 20xx | 4 (`00`), 5 (`49`), 8 (`09`) | Determined identically (00–69 → 20xx; transform.py: `y < 50` → `2000+y`). |\n| B4c | **Two-digit years 50–69** | 2 (`55`), 7 (`69`), 10 (`50`) | **DETERMINED DIFFERENTLY.** migrate.md: 00–69 → 20xx, so 55→2055, 69→2069, 50→2050. transform.py: `y >= 50` → `1900+y`, so 55→1955, 69→1969, 50→1950. |\n| B5 | **Surrounding whitespace on the input string** | 5 (`\" 8/15/49 \"`) | **UNDETERMINED by migrate.md.** The spec defines the legacy form as `M/D/YY` / `M/D/YYYY` and never mentions whitespace; an implementation authored solely from migrate.md may equally strip it, tolerate it (Python `int()` accepts surrounding whitespace in components), or reject the input. transform.py determines it: it strips and returns `2049-08-15`. |\n| B6 | Leading zeros inside components (`07`, `04`, `01`, `00`, `09`) | 3, 4, 8, 10 | Determined identically: migrate.md allows two-digit components (so `07` is the two-digit month 7, `00` the two-digit year 0); transform.py integer-parses them to the same values. |\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **Determined differently — two-digit-year century pivot for years 50–69**\n   (behavior B4c): migrate.md maps 50–69 to 20xx; transform.py maps them to\n   19xx. Exercised by probes **2, 7, 10**. On these probes migrate.md\n   determines `2055-03-07`, `2069-05-05`, `2050-04-01` respectively, while\n   transform.py returns `1955-03-07`, `1969-05-05`, `1950-04-01`.\n2. **Undetermined — surrounding-whitespace handling** (behavior B5):\n   exercised by probe **5** (`\" 8/15/49 \"`). migrate.md does not determine\n   whether such input is accepted, trimmed, or rejected; transform.py strips\n   and returns `2049-08-15`.\n\n## Completeness argument\n\nEvery probe is a three-component `/`-separated string; no probe exercises\nalternative separators, missing/extra components, non-numeric components,\nout-of-range calendar values (all month values 1–12, all day values valid for\ntheir month), negative numbers, three-digit years, or empty input. Therefore\nthe probe-exercised behavior set is exactly B1–B6 above: B1–B3, B4a, B4b, and\nB6 are determined identically by both artifacts; B4c is determined\ndifferently; B5 is undetermined by migrate.md. No further divergent or\nundetermined probe-exercised behavior exists.\n\nNote: which probe indices actually diverge in the final deliverable is\nreserved to the admissible E-B comparison (isolated clean-room implementation\nvs transform.py); this E-A statement predicts the behavior classes only.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":782,"cache_read_input_tokens":42006,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":782},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8dde847-f1a1-4b0b-b810-94d75dff6683","uuid":"77402454-eb25-4048-8ed8-363f3df25db0","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:02:08.673Z","request_id":"req_011CdsXmKiyF4yiBAfvUTRhB"}
