{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdsY4mqpjVEtb5HdPadjT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stage S6 is complete. I executed the two in-session nodes of the `isolated-child` harness and produced all deliverables; the session ends here, with realization, integration, and verification left to the root harness.\n\n**What the analysis found (E-A, resolving Q1):** migrate.md and transform.py disagree on exactly one probe-exercised behavior — the two-digit-year century pivot. migrate.md maps 00–69 to 20xx, while transform.py maps years ≥ 50 to 19xx, so years 50–69 diverge; probes 2 (`3/7/55`), 7 (`5/5/69`), and 10 (`4/01/50`) exercise this. One behavior is left undetermined by migrate.md: surrounding-whitespace handling, exercised by probe 5 (`\" 8/15/49 \"`), which transform.py strips. Every other behavior the 12 probes exercise (parsing, zero-padding, four-digit pass-through, the 00–49 and 70–99 mappings, leading zeros) is determined identically; `ea-behavior-statement.md` carries the full per-probe enumeration and completeness argument.\n\n**What stays pending, and why:** Q2 (the clean-room comparison, E-B) requires an author who has never accessed transform.py — a condition this session violated the moment it read the package — so it is honestly `UNRESOLVED`. Q3's verdict follows jointly from E-A and E-B, so `result.json` carries `verdict: PENDING-INTEGRATION` and `divergent_probe_indices: PENDING-INTEGRATION`.\n\n**The proposed child bundle** (under `child/`, all five files crossing the `propose-child` event at authoring time):\n- **Input manifest contains only `package/artifacts/migrate.md`** — probes.json is deliberately withheld so the child cannot be nudged toward whitespace handling by seeing probe 5, keeping the undetermined-behavior test clean.\n- The child contract sits exactly at the K-E6-child-max envelope (Read+Write, terminal, 1 model call); the harness is instantiated from the template.\n- The prompt instructs a literal implementation of the spec as `child_transform.py` exposing `transform(s)`, with no mention of any other trial artifact.\n- `integration-plan.json` pre-commits a judgment-free rule: per-probe string comparison of the two implementations (exception on exactly one side counts as divergent), verdict `DIVERGES` iff the divergent set is non-empty.\n\nThe ledger records the `observe-evidence` and `propose-child` node events plus two creator bookkeeping propose events (the E-A writeup, since the observe node holds no Write tool, and the universal deliverables). Based on E-A alone I expect the eventual verdict to be `DIVERGES` on probes 2, 7, 10 — but that prediction is deliberately kept out of the child's inputs and the pending result fields."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1168,"cache_read_input_tokens":63914,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1168},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8dde847-f1a1-4b0b-b810-94d75dff6683","uuid":"ae6ea144-0e97-4e88-9998-7cc67b192359","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:03:48.268Z","request_id":"req_011CdsY4kYSW7y9WzbjW7Pwh"}
